                            <comment id="16619633" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 18 Sep 2018 19:57:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jooger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jooger&quot;&gt;jooger&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
Unfortunately with recent changes to MVCC things are not that easy anymore and there is not global &quot;mvcc enabled&quot; flag. Instead, this flag is governed on per-cache basis. So we need to check whether SQL is allowed to participated in transaction on per-cache basis. I think &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=rkondakov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;rkondakov&quot;&gt;rkondakov&lt;/a&gt; could show you relevant pieces of code where it should be done.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16620737" author="jooger" created="Wed, 19 Sep 2018 15:14:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vozerov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vozerov&quot;&gt;vozerov&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the review and good point to fix. Fix has been done and tet result looks good.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test results: &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=1906467&amp;amp;tab=queuedBuildOverviewTab&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=1906467&amp;amp;tab=queuedBuildOverviewTab&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16630525" author="vozerov" created="Thu, 27 Sep 2018 14:31:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jooger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jooger&quot;&gt;jooger&lt;/a&gt;, patch looks good, but lets do the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Improve error message a bit. It should explain what kind of caches are not allowed to have DML inside ongoing transaction, and second - we need to explain users how to override this.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let&apos;s merge with master again and re-run tests to make sure that SQL tests are OK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Proposed error message: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
DML statements are not allowed inside a transaction over cache(s) with TRANSACTIONAL atomicity mode (change atomicity mode to TRANSACTIONAL_SNAPSHOT or disable &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt; error message with system property &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;-DIGNITE_ALLOW_DML_INSIDE_TRANSACTION=&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&quot;&lt;/span&gt;) [cacheName=...])
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16631421" author="nizhikov" created="Fri, 28 Sep 2018 06:32:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jooger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jooger&quot;&gt;jooger&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vozerov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vozerov&quot;&gt;vozerov&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=mcherkasov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;mcherkasov&quot;&gt;mcherkasov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can we move this ticket to 2.8?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16631973" author="vozerov" created="Fri, 28 Sep 2018 15:02:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Let&apos;s move to AI 2.8. We have a slight chance to finalize it by Monday (including tests, another review, etc), but not sure.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16683371" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 12 Nov 2018 08:12:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jooger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jooger&quot;&gt;jooger&lt;/a&gt;, my comments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) We do not need collection of cache names. It is enough to check for active transaction only once when the very first non-MVCC cache is found &lt;br/&gt;
2) Incorrect test suite was picked (Queries 4 is for failover continuous queries tests)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I fixed both problems. Please review my change. If agree, we need to re-run tests on TC and get TCBot&apos;s visa.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
